From 4533b6197661f13624405e2f492a877c390efcad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 13:39:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: stale-role JWT bug + remove debug leftovers
 (alert/console.log) in AdminCafes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- middleware/auth.ts: authenticate() now re-fetches the user's current
  role and isActive status from the DB on every request instead of
  trusting the JWT payload's role for the full 7-day token lifetime.
  This is what was causing '+998913472886' to keep showing role:
  CUSTOMER after being promoted to CAFE_OWNER — the old token was
  still around. Also means a deactivated user is locked out
  immediately, not after their token happens to expire.
- api/client.ts + AdminPages.tsx: getAdminCafes() had no return type,
  so the caller defensively tried result.data?.cafes || result.cafes
  || result.data (a symptom of not knowing the real shape). Backend
  actually returns a flat { cafes, pagination }. Typed the call
  properly and simplified the caller to match.
- Removed a leftover alert('ADMIN CAFES ISHLAYAPTI') that was firing
  on every visit to the admin cafes list in production, plus a stray
  console.log in cafe creation.
